  "behavior": [
    "Accepted-owner observation and canonical withdrawal history are enumerated on one repeatable-read connection with independent scoped family counts, exact stored identity/digest checks and pure lifecycle validation.",
    "Additive GET register-observations/lifecycle returns scope, observation time, original receipt/draft, active/superseded/withdrawn status and withdrawal metadata. It exposes no idempotency key or mutation authority; draft confirmations reset.",
    "Legacy list keeps its path/schema/projection with no withdrawals. Any withdrawal in scope gives safe409 lifecycle_upgrade_required; malformed, missing or partial storage gives503 instead of captured-empty.",
    "Generated transport validates scoped identities, complete lineage and exact microsecond receipt chronology. New UI requires lifecycle support, shows retained withdrawn facts, disables historical correction and selects only active references for corporate-event presentation/transport.",
    "Current source preview, guarded source readiness, annual readiness and review reject an unavailable active observation before downstream work. Historical capture receipts remain distinct from currentness."
  ],
